      "stageRecord": "The sentence has a clitic-climbing reading: Giulia wants to read the entity represented by accusative lo. Whether lo refers to a masculine individual or a masculine thing does not change the syntax. This analysis adopts a GB restructuring treatment that retains an infinitival IP with controlled PRO; restructuring will make that complement transparent specifically for clitic displacement. First, leggere selects lo as its internal argument and assigns it the Theme role and accusative Case. The clitic is represented as a minimal pronominal NP, capable of occupying a clitic position at its eventual host. Second, the infinitival predicate assigns its external role to PRO. Third, vuole selects the infinitival IP as its propositional argument and assigns its external role to Giulia through VP predication. Fourth, Giulia obligatorily controls PRO, identifying the intended reader with the person who wants. PRO is unpronounced and ungoverned in the nonfinite subject position; it is not a trace of Giulia. Finally, finite I licenses nominative Case on Giulia and agrees with it in the third-person singular. The lexical form vuole is entered already inflected; this analysis does not decompose its spelling into separate terminals. Giulia is base-generated in the matrix subject position, following the classical GB subject configuration rather than a VP-internal-subject derivation. The current order is a pre-movement representation, not the surface order.",
