      "stageRecord": "First, vuole raises from the matrix V position shown previously and adjoins to finite I, leaving a silent verbal trace. This is ordinary V-to-I head movement: the finite verb locally supports the tense and agreement specification, while its trace preserves the lexical predicate's complement relation. The movement does not create a new spelling or fuse separately pronounced morphemes; vuole remains the same whole-word terminal. Second, the restructuring use of volere licenses the matrix predicate and its infinitival complement as a single domain for clitic placement. This is a construction-specific transparency relation, not a claim that every infinitival complement permits climbing. The analysis retains the embedded IP and the control dependency rather than deleting PRO or reassigning its theta-role. Transparency for clitic displacement is distinguished from government into the embedded subject position, so PRO remains ungoverned. No embedded CP barrier is projected. The object clitic is still in the complement position of leggere, making its source explicit before its displacement.",
