      "stageRecord": "First, lo moves from the complement of leggere to a left-adjoined clitic position at matrix I, leaving a silent NP trace. This analysis uses the GB clitic-adjunction convention: the minimal pronominal NP occupies a position attached to the inflectional head. It treats this as a special clitic-chain dependency licensed by restructuring, not as ordinary V-to-I movement or as movement of the infinitive. The earlier restructuring relation permits the dependency across the retained infinitival IP. The chain receives its Theme interpretation and accusative Case at its lower position; lo is therefore the object of leggere, not an independently selected object of vuole. Second, the lower trace is properly governed by the adjacent lexical verb leggere, satisfying the relevant empty-category requirement. Third, the displaced clitic is licensed as a proclitic on the finite host vuole, which gives lo vuole rather than an enclitic form on leggere. Finally, the referential clitic is free in its local embedded binding domain: PRO does not bind it, and obligatory control consequently excludes an interpretation on which lo is a reflexive object referring back to Giulia. Giulia and PRO remain distinct thematic arguments linked by control. The resulting pronounced sequence is exactly Giulia lo vuole leggere.",
